Subject: [flux] Hide Chromium's avatar button

The toolbar showed two account controls at once: Flux's own, in the tab strip
(patch 0010), and Chromium's, offering "Sign in to Chromium?" next to it.

The second one cannot work. Signing in needs the Google OAuth client id and
secret the fork does not ship - the browser says so itself at startup,
"Desktop Identity Consistency cannot be enabled as no OAuth client ID and
client secret have been configured" - so the button is a dead offer that also
names the wrong product.

Hidden rather than removed. ToolbarView holds `avatar_` by pointer and reads
it for flex order, margins and the overflow menu's insertion index; an
invisible avatar button is a state upstream already produces whenever
CanShowForProfile() is false, so this is the supported way to be rid of it.

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar/toolbar_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar/toolbar_view.cc
@@ -574,9 +574,18 @@
   if (!features::IsWebUIAvatarButtonEnabled()) {
     avatar_ =
         AddChildView(std::make_unique<AvatarToolbarButton>(browser_view_));
-    bool show_avatar_toolbar_button =
-        AvatarToolbarButtonInterface::CanShowForProfile(browser_->GetProfile());
-    avatar_->SetVisible(show_avatar_toolbar_button);
+    // Never shown in Flux. The browser has its own account control in the tab
+    // strip (patch 0010), and Chromium's is a second one offering "Sign in to
+    // Chromium?" - an offer this build cannot honour, because signing in needs
+    // the Google API keys the fork deliberately does not ship. Two avatars
+    // side by side, one of them dead and naming the wrong product.
+    //
+    // The button is still constructed rather than skipped: ToolbarView looks
+    // it up by pointer in half a dozen places (flex order, margins, the
+    // overflow menu's insertion index), and an invisible button is a state
+    // upstream already supports - it is what CanShowForProfile() returning
+    // false produces.
+    avatar_->SetVisible(false);
   }
 
   overflow_button_ = AddChildView(std::make_unique<OverflowButton>());
